  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following lines correctly show the temperature dependence of equilibrium constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo></math> for an exothermic reaction?<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0082_cfba365da626.png\" style=\"width: 259px; height: 235px;\" /><br />&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The Arrhenius equation in Logarithmic form:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>In</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mi>RT</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p>On comparing with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>mx</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p>For an exothermic reaction, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, slope will be positive and the intercept can be either positive or negative.</p>"
  }
